<section class="hero"><div class="wrap">
<p class="kick">Leather &middot; Make &middot; Care</p>
<h1>The bag is the leather and the stitching. Everything else is a label.</h1>
<p class="lead">Monogra is an independent guide to leather bags. Three free tools and two long guides on what each leather actually is, how much a bag really holds, and the construction details that give quality away.</p>
<p class="hero-cta"><a class="btn" href="#tools">Open the tools</a> <a class="btn gh" href="leather-care-guide.html">Read the care guide</a></p>
<figure class="hero-fig"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1792066329499-97aa32997438?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1400&q=75" alt="A person in a velvet top holding a tan suede handbag" width="1400" height="600" fetchpriority="high"></figure></div></section>
<section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap">
<div class="four">
<div><b>8</b><p>leather types explained</p></div><div><b>9</b><p>construction checks</p></div><div><b>0</b><p>affiliate links</p></div><div><b>Free</b><p>no sign-up, ever</p></div></div></div></section>
<section><div class="wrap"><div class="sec-h"><p class="rule">Where to start</p><h2>Four things that decide how a bag ages</h2><p>None of them are visible in a product photograph, which is why so many expensive bags disappoint and so many modest ones do not.</p></div>
<div class="cards">
<div><h3>1. Which layer of the hide</h3><p>Full-grain keeps the hide&#8217;s own surface and gets better with use. Split and corrected leathers are sanded and coated, so they start at their best and slowly wear through.</p>
<h3 style="margin-top:1.4em">2. How the edges are finished</h3><p>Painted or folded edges take time and skill. Raw, fuzzy edges are where a cheap bag shows itself first, usually within a year.</p></div>
<div><h3>3. What happens at stress points</h3><p>Handles, strap anchors and base corners carry the load. Reinforcement, backing and a tight stitch line there matter more than anything on the front panel.</p>
<h3 style="margin-top:1.4em">4. The weight of the hardware</h3><p>Solid metal feels cold and heavy and keeps running for decades. Plated zinc feels light, warms up in the hand and wears through at the edges.</p></div>
</div></div></section>
<section class="tools" id="tools"><div class="wrap">
<div class="sec-h"><p class="rule" style="color:#B99653">Free tools</p><h2>Three questions, answered here</h2><p>Everything runs in your browser. Nothing is saved and nothing is sent anywhere.</p></div>
<div class="tool" id="leather"><h3>Leather Type Decoder</h3><p>Choose what the label says and see what it really is, how to care for it and how it will age.</p>
<div class="tool-grid"><div><div class="fld"><label for="lth">What does the label say?</label><select id="lth"><option value="fullgrain">Full-grain leather</option><option value="topgrain">Top-grain / calf leather</option><option value="saffiano">Saffiano or cross-hatch</option><option value="suede">Suede or nubuck</option><option value="patent">Patent leather</option><option value="canvas">Coated canvas</option><option value="exotic">Embossed grain</option><option value="vegan">Vegan / PU leather</option></select></div>
<figure style="margin:0"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1702325107940-88f9cd4468c2?auto=format&fit=crop&w=700&q=75" alt="A black purse sitting on a table" width="700" height="470" loading="lazy" style="aspect-ratio:3/2;object-fit:cover"></figure></div>
<div class="out" id="ltOut"></div></div></div>
<div class="tool" id="size"><h3>Capacity Calculator</h3><p>Three measurements and we will tell you what the bag will actually hold.</p>
<div class="tool-grid"><div><div class="fgrid"><div class="fld"><label for="bW">Width (cm)</label><input id="bW" type="number" min="5" max="70" value="28"></div>
<div class="fld"><label for="bH">Height (cm)</label><input id="bH" type="number" min="5" max="60" value="20"></div></div>
<div class="fgrid"><div class="fld"><label for="bD">Depth (cm)</label><input id="bD" type="number" min="2" max="40" value="11"></div>
<div class="fld"><label for="bUse">Mainly for</label><select id="bUse"><option value="day">Everyday carry</option><option value="work">Work and a laptop</option><option value="evening">An evening out</option><option value="travel">Travel</option></select></div></div>
<figure style="margin:0"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1760624294514-3548bee70d26?auto=format&fit=crop&w=700&q=75" alt="A person wearing a cream-coloured crossbody bag" width="700" height="470" loading="lazy" style="aspect-ratio:3/2;object-fit:cover"></figure></div>
<div class="out" id="bOut"></div></div></div>
<div class="tool" id="check"><h3>Quality Checklist</h3><p>Nine construction checks you can make in a shop or from good photographs. This is about make, not about authenticity.</p>
<div class="tool-grid"><div>
<label class="chk"><input id="q0" type="checkbox">Stitching is even, straight and tight, with no loose threads</label><label class="chk"><input id="q1" type="checkbox">Hardware feels heavy and cold, and the zip runs smoothly both ways</label><label class="chk"><input id="q2" type="checkbox">The lining is stitched in neatly and sits flat</label><label class="chk"><input id="q3" type="checkbox">Edges are painted or folded cleanly, with no raw fuzz</label><label class="chk"><input id="q4" type="checkbox">Branding is crisp, level and correctly spelled</label><label class="chk"><input id="q5" type="checkbox">The smell is leather or nothing, not strong glue or plastic</label><label class="chk"><input id="q6" type="checkbox">The price is far below anything comparable from the same maker</label><label class="chk"><input id="q7" type="checkbox">The seller cannot show the inside, the base or the hardware close up</label><label class="chk"><input id="q8" type="checkbox">The dust bag, card or packaging looks newer than the bag</label>
<figure style="margin:.8em 0 0"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1727414782567-0ec8a4eb6096?auto=format&fit=crop&w=700&q=75" alt="A close view of a bag with a metal handle" width="700" height="470" loading="lazy" style="aspect-ratio:3/2;object-fit:cover"></figure></div>
<div class="out" id="chkOut"></div></div></div>
</div></section>
<section class="band"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1780679024697-a18a3484c117?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1600&q=75" alt="" width="1600" height="900" loading="lazy">
<div class="wrap"><p class="kick">A word about authenticity</p><h2>No website can authenticate a bag</h2>
<p>Counterfeits now copy the visible details well enough that photograph-based checks fail regularly. Our checklist tells you about construction quality. For origin, go to the brand or an accredited specialist, and buy from sellers who accept returns.</p></div></section>
<section><div class="wrap"><div class="sec-h"><p class="rule">Long reads</p><h2>Two guides, start to finish</h2></div>
<div class="cards">
<article class="card"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1758817862631-f4a11090a2f6?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=75" alt="A person holding a stylish handbag" width="800" height="533" loading="lazy"><div class="cb"><p class="kick">Guide one</p><h3>The Leather Care Guide</h3><p>Cleaning, conditioning, water marks, scratches, storage and the mistakes that ruin good leather. Plus what to do when something goes wrong.</p><p><a class="btn gh" href="leather-care-guide.html">Read the guide</a></p></div></article>
<article class="card"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1792768271766-6c098311d036?auto=format&fit=crop&w=800&q=75" alt="A person on a sofa holding a bag" width="800" height="533" loading="lazy"><div class="cb"><p class="kick">Guide two</p><h3>The Bag Buying Guide</h3><p>Construction, hardware, linings, sizing for real life, what price actually buys you, and how to shop second-hand without being caught out.</p><p><a class="btn gh" href="bag-buying-guide.html">Read the guide</a></p></div></article>
</div></div></section>
<section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap"><div class="sec-h"><p class="rule">Questions</p><h2>Asked all the time</h2></div>
<div class="faq"><details><summary>What is the difference between full-grain and genuine leather?</summary><p>Full-grain is the outer surface of the hide with its natural texture intact, and it is the strongest leather there is. &ldquo;Genuine leather&rdquo; is a grading term for lower layers of the hide, often sanded and coated. The phrase sounds reassuring and sits near the bottom of the quality ladder.</p></details><details><summary>How can I tell a well-made bag from a badly made one?</summary><p>Look at the parts nobody photographs: the inside of the zip, the base corners, the stitch line where the handle meets the body, and the edges. Even stitching, clean painted edges and hardware that feels cold and heavy are consistent signs of care.</p></details><details><summary>Can a checklist tell me whether a bag is authentic?</summary><p>No. Construction tells you about quality, not origin, and counterfeits have become very good at the visible details. Authentication is a job for the brand or an accredited specialist, and buying from a seller who accepts returns protects you far better than any list.</p></details><details><summary>How often should leather be conditioned?</summary><p>Two or three times a year for untreated or full-grain leather, less in humid climates. Coated leathers such as saffiano and patent need none at all. Over-conditioning is a real problem: it softens the structure and leaves a tacky surface that attracts dirt.</p></details><details><summary>Does an expensive bag last longer?</summary><p>Not automatically. Price reflects brand, materials and marketing in unpredictable proportions. A mid-priced bag in full-grain leather with even stitching and solid hardware will usually outlast a far more expensive one made from coated split leather.</p></details></div></div></section>
<section class="nl"><div class="wrap"><p class="kick">Newsletter</p><h2>The Monogra Letter</h2>
<p>One short email a month: a leather explained, a care mistake worth avoiding, and anything new in the guides. No spam, unsubscribe any time.</p>
<p><a class="btn" style="background:#B99653;color:#2B2320" href="mailto:hello@monogra.com?subject=The%20Monogra%20Letter&body=Please%20subscribe%20me.">Subscribe by email</a></p>
